i'd like to propose a new spellbook: the spellbook of apply curse
which could be used to selectively curse items.  

the motivation is that i just ascended a rogue, but found not 1
potion of unholy water.  i also found no cursed scrolls of gold
detection, a necessity in my eyes for the elemental planes.  i only
had a blessed magic marker, and had no wishes left (except wishing
in my own mind that i could find some damn way to curse the scrolls
of gold detection i had :), so had no way of writing the thing (i
detest polypiling in general, so didn't want to pile all those tools
in hopes of getting a cursed, or at least uncursed, magic marker).
my solution was to drop everything but my armor, my weapon, and the
scrolls, and wait for the wiz to appear.  he double-troubled, and
eventually i got my cursed scrolls, but in the mean-time everything
else i had was cursed also.  this was easily remedied with a blessed 
scroll of remove curse (for the armor & weapon), but it was sort
of a pain killing the 2 wiz's.  anyway, it just seems that there is
some sort of imbalance in the blessing/cursing.  it's relatively
easy to bless things, while quite hard to curse them.  just my
$.02.

btw, i've always thought it was a bit silly that you can do some
things with cursed items which don't cause them to stick to your
hands, e.g. throwing cursed weapons, or applying cursed tools
(magic marker, key, ...).  

